@VivixLabs_HQ These look really cool, but what I really like is the ability to interact with them.

For example, you can use one as a tutor and have it respond in real time to your questions to guide a lesson. 

The first company that does this will print money, for sure.

The economics of agentic AI matter as much as the technology.

If an existing ChatGPT plan can support specialized agents in different roles, companies can test agentic workflows without adding another AI subscription to the stack.

@hyperagentapp #HyperagentPartner

@giacomomasseron Depends on the problem and the consequences.

One workflow deletes unsolicited emails. I proceed only with 90%+ confidence.

Another workflow labels promotions and ad emails in my inbox. I proceed with anything about 60% confidence.

@julesmalin For some of my workflows, I review low-confidence results. For other workflows, I just ignore them.

For example, I have a workflow to screen out any solicitation emails. They aren't spam, but I don't want to worry about them either.

I classify them, and anything above 90% goes to the trash. Anything lower than 90% stays in my inbox.

